# Built-in display UI resolution (More Space), keyed by panel size.
# macconfig-check.sh reads the built-in panel's spdisplays_pixelresolution
# (for example spdisplays_3024x1964Retina), picks the matching row, and warns
# when _spdisplays_resolution does not start with that row's prefix. A panel
# size not listed here, or no built-in panel (clamshell), is an info line.
# macos.sh uses displayplacer to apply the matching mode on the built-in
# panel only. A missing mode stays by hand.
# Format: panel | More Space prefix
3024x1964|1800 x 1169
3456x2234|2056 x 1329

# ARZOPA 16.1" portable USB-C monitor. When it is not connected the check is
# an info line, not drift. macos.sh sets the mode with displayplacer.
# Match the name, the serial, or the type. The persistent screen id is not a match
# key: on pdone-mac2 it was 82BDB23E-5EA1-4C6F-925B-EB392903EC5E, and
# macOS mints a new one when the same panel is plugged into another USB-C
# port. The name ARZOPA is what system_profiler and Hammerspoon both report.
# The serial s74646035 is displayplacer's serial screen id and stays with the
# panel. Type is "16 inch external screen", and it counts only when that
# displayplacer block has no different name and no different serial.
# place "left" means origin (-width, 0). The laptop display stays at (0,0),
# so it stays the main display (Dock and menu bar) and the tops line up.
# hz is the preferred refresh rate. Plugged straight into the MacBook the
# ARZOPA offers 180Hz. Through the StarTech Thunderbolt 5 dock
# (215-TB5USB4DOCK) 1920x1080 unscaled only goes up to 144Hz. When hz is not
# listed at that resolution and scaling, the highest rate that is listed
# there is expected instead, and macos.sh sets it.
# Format: external | name | serial | type | res | hz | scaling | place
external|ARZOPA|s74646035|16 inch external screen|1920x1080|180|off|left
